================================================================================
## Clear new Dependabot alerts: pyasn1, graphql-core, joserfc
================================================================================

Context: New Dependabot alerts appeared on `uv.lock` / `src/mcp-server/uv.lock`
— pyasn1 0.6.4 (#313-#316, #320-#323, quadratic BER/CER/DER, BIT STRING, REAL,
and ANY decoding DoS), graphql-core 3.3.0 (#319, memory leak on aborted
validations), and joserfc 1.6.8 / 1.7.1 (#309-#312, unbounded JWE
`recipients` array CPU exhaustion + compact-JWS size-guard allocation before
rejection). All three are transitive (pyasn1 via pyasn1-modules/rsa/
google-auth; graphql-core via strawberry-graphql; joserfc via
authlib/fastmcp-slim) and had no explicit floor yet (pyasn1 was floored at
the previous, now-insufficient, patched version). Ported the same fix applied
to the `0.9.2` branch. `oauthlib>=4.0.0` (#175/#176/#282/#318) remains
blocked: `databricks-sql-connector` 4.4–4.6 pins `oauthlib>=3.1.0,<4.0.0`,
so it cannot be raised without breaking the Databricks SQL connector; left as
a documented accepted risk.

Changes:

1. pyproject.toml
   Raise `pyasn1` floor to `>=0.6.5`; add `graphql-core>=3.3.1` and
   `joserfc>=1.7.6` constraint floors with Dependabot alert references.
2. src/mcp-server/pyproject.toml
   Same `pyasn1>=0.6.5` raise and new `joserfc>=1.7.6` floor (no
   graphql-core/strawberry-graphql dependency in this subpackage).
3. uv.lock
   Regenerated against the Databricks PyPI proxy (`pypi.org` is not reachable
   from this sandbox network), then rewrote `registry =
   "https://pypi-proxy.dev.databricks.com/simple"` → `"https://pypi.org/simple"`
   and `https://pypi-proxy.dev.databricks.com/packages/` →
   `https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/` across the file (the proxy
   mirrors PyPI's own `/packages/<hash>/<hash>/filename` layout 1:1, so the
   rewrite is a pure identity substitution — confirmed by `uv sync --frozen`
   downloading and installing the rewritten URLs successfully). Verified zero
   `pypi-proxy` references remain and `UV_INDEX_URL=https://pypi.org/simple
   uv lock --check` passes.
4. src/mcp-server/uv.lock
   Same regeneration + URL rewrite for the standalone MCP graph.
5. docs/development.md
   Add `pyasn1>=0.6.5`, `graphql-core>=3.3.1`, `joserfc>=1.7.6` to the
   current explicit security floors list.

