## Fix Apps deploy: drop default identity scopes from user_api_scopes
================================================================================

Context: `make deploy` of a fresh instance failed at app creation with
`POST /api/2.0/apps → 400 INVALID_PARAMETER_VALUE: The specified scope
iam.current-user:read is not a valid scope`. Databricks Apps now treats the two
identity scopes (`iam.current-user:read`, `iam.access-control:read`) as
non-selectable platform defaults — they are auto-assigned when no scopes are
requested and the create API rejects them when listed explicitly (confirmed in
the AWS/Azure "Configure authorization in a Databricks app" docs). Only
additional scopes such as `sql` may be declared. Removed the two identity
scopes from every `user_api_scopes` declaration, keeping just `sql` (admin
group checks / MCP OBO, #208); the identity defaults are still applied
automatically.

Changes:

1. databricks.yml
   Both app resources (`ontobricks_dev_app`, `mcp_ontobricks_app`):
   `user_api_scopes` reduced to `[sql]` (dropped the two identity scopes),
   with an explaining comment.
2. app.yaml.template
   `authorization.user.scopes` reduced to `[sql]`; comment rewritten to note
   the identity scopes are platform defaults that must not be declared.
   (`app.yaml` itself is generated from this template and gitignored.)

Modified files:
- databricks.yml
- app.yaml.template
- changelogs/v0.10.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-11-03.log

Deployment: `make deploy` (target dev-lakebase-10x) succeeded end-to-end after
the fix — both apps RUNNING/ACTIVE, `/healthz` → 200, Lakebase schema
`ontobricks_demo_10_registry_sc` initialized and UC/Lakebase grants applied to
both app service principals. Also required an unrelated environment fix
(re-auth of the expired `DEFAULT` OAuth CLI profile) and the account admin
freeing service-principal quota (50k users+SP account cap).

