## Persist last hypothetical-facts prompt on the scenario
================================================================================

Context: Simulation → Scenarios → Hypothetical facts has a "Describe the facts"
textarea used by Propose facts. The agent rewrote General → Description, but the
prompt itself was never stored on the spec, so reopening a scenario left the box
empty (or showed another scenario's leftover text). Persist `fact_prompt` with
the spec, restore it on load, and quiet-save after a propose when the scenario
already exists.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/simulation/Spec.py
   Add `fact_prompt` (max 4000 chars) to parse/serialize; omitted/empty stays "".
2. src/front/static/simulation/js/simulation-workbench.js
   Collect and restore `fact_prompt`; after Propose facts, quiet-save the last
   prompt (and current spec) when the scenario already has an id.
3. tests/units/simulation/test_simulation_core.py
   Round-trip and length-cap coverage for `fact_prompt`.
4. tests/units/front/test_simulation_page_contract.py
   Contract that load/collect/persist wire `simWbFactPrompt`.
5. docs/user-guide.md
   Note that the last proposed wording is stored with the scenario.

